string getSupervisorMaterials(string supervisorId, string skipLinesTxt)
{
	// PAGED BY Issue_Line ROW. skipLinesTxt is how many of this supervisor's
	// Issue_Lines to skip before processing; the call then processes up to
	// ROW_BUDGET more and stops, reporting linesConsumed so the widget can call
	// again with skipLines + linesConsumed. linesConsumed == 0 means done.
	//
	// WHY BY LINE, NOT BY VOUCHER: an old chunked handover left 1800+ rows in a
	// single Material_Issue subform. Paging by voucher would still hand one call
	// that whole subform and blow the statement-execution limit on it. Paging by
	// line caps the work per call whatever the voucher shape.
	//
	// FIRST PAGE ONLY (skipLines == 0) also returns the supervisor picker, the
	// waste list, plansAssigned and the disputes netting - all bounded, none
	// needing to repeat. Later pages return materials/printedPieces only, plus
	// the running cursor. plansAwaiting is derived by the widget from planFed
	// (the plan ids each page saw material for), unioned across pages.
	//
	// Empty skipLinesTxt == first page.
	// Supervisor's material receipt list - everything issued to him that he has not
	// confirmed yet.
	//
	// The list is of PHYSICAL THINGS, not order lines. One 10m roll booked against
	// three items is one line here, because he measures the roll once. The per-order
	// split is nested inside for the exception path, where he received less than was
	// issued and has to decide which order goes short.
	//
	// Waste pieces are the exception to that: a specific 300x400 remnant was cut for
	// a specific item, so it is not fungible and gets its own line.
	//
	// supervisorId empty -> returns just the supervisor list, so the widget can
	// populate its picker with one call.
	//
	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// READS THE HANDOVER RECORDS DIRECTLY. This function used to reconstruct the
	// list by walking every open plan in the org, then every Material_Requirement
	// row on it, then re-attaching lots from the vouchers - three unbounded scans
	// on a screen showing one person's deliveries. On a busy floor that blew the
	// statement-execution limit, which is NOT catchable: it kills the script and
	// the widget gets a bare "code 9430" with no error card.
	//
	// The handover record already IS the receipt list. Material_Issue is one row
	// per press of Issue, Issue_Lines one row per requirement it fed, and each
	// line carries Qty, Lot, Cut size, Requirement, Plan_Item and Settled_Qty.
	// "Not confirmed yet" is simply Settled_Qty < Qty. receiveMaterials already
	// works this way (it settles Settled_Qty on these same lines), so the read
	// side now matches the write side and the two cannot disagree.
	//
	// BOUNDS, all off the supervisor id, none off a plan walk:
	//   Material_Issue[Issued_To == supId]          - his handovers
	//   Waste_Movement[Moved_By == supId]           - his remnant hand-overs
	//   Stock_Dispute[Supervisor == supId]          - his open disputes
	//   Production_Planning[Assigned_To == supId]   - his plans, for the badge
	//                                                 counts only, no row walk
	// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

	supJson = "";
	matJson = "";
	wasteJson = "";

	// SUPERVISORS ONLY, but every supervisor - not only those with something
	// pending.
	//
	// This picker stands in for a login until zoho.loginuser can be resolved to
	// an Employee record. Two different filters get confused here, so both are
	// stated:
	//
	//  BY WORK - never. A login does not appear and disappear depending on
	//  whether you have work waiting; a supervisor with an empty day still has
	//  to sign in and look at his production tab.
	//
	//  BY ROLE - yes, now that Designation exists. Offering a store person or a
	//  dispatcher as someone to "log in as" was only ever a symptom of having no
	//  role field to filter on. This is the login stand-in, so the list is who
	//  may hold this screen.
	//
	// Matched on the Designation TEXT. It is a dropdown whose choices are built
	// at runtime from the Department, so there is no lookup id to resolve - see
	// autoPopulateDesignation.
	supEmps = Employee[Designation == "Supervisor" && Status == "Active"] sort by Employee_Name;

	// FALLS BACK TO EVERYONE IF THAT FINDS NOBODY, deliberately, and this is not
	// belt-and-braces - it is the difference between a screen that works and a
	// dead one. Designation and Status are new fields; every Employee record
	// created before them is blank on both, so the moment this filter shipped it
	// would have emptied the picker and locked every supervisor out of the
	// widget with nothing on screen explaining why.
	//
	// Degrades to exactly the old behaviour, which was usable. Once the employee
	// records carry designations the fallback stops firing on its own, and the
	// info line below is how you tell which state you are in.
	if(supEmps.count() == 0)
	{
		info "getSupervisorMaterials: no Active employee has Designation 'Supervisor' - falling back to the full employee list. Set Designation and Status on the Employee records.";
		supEmps = Employee[ID != 0] sort by Employee_Name;
	}

	for each  emp in supEmps
	{
		if(supJson != "")
		{
			supJson = supJson + ",";
		}
		// IDs forced to string - 18-digit ids break JSON.parse otherwise.
		supJson = supJson + "{\"id\":\"" + emp.ID + "\",\"name\":\"" + ifnull(emp.Employee_Name,"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + "\"}";
	}

	if(supervisorId == null || supervisorId.trim() == "")
	{
		return "{\"errors\":[],\"supervisors\":[" + supJson + "],\"materials\":[],\"waste\":[],\"printedPieces\":[],\"planFed\":[],\"plansAssigned\":0,\"linesConsumed\":0,\"skipLines\":0}";
	}

	supId = supervisorId.trim().toLong();

	skipLines = 0;
	slStr = ifnull(skipLinesTxt,"").toString().trim();
	if(slStr != "")
	{
		skipLines = slStr.toLong();
		if(skipLines < 0)
		{
			skipLines = 0;
		}
	}
	firstPage = (skipLines == 0);
	rowBudget = 150;

	printedPiecesJson = "";
	// plan ids this page saw material issued for - unioned by the widget across
	// pages, then subtracted from plansAssigned to get plansAwaiting.
	planFedJson = "";
	planFedSeen = List();

	// Same debug wrapper the other functions carry - Creator collapses every
	// runtime failure into "code 9430", so surface the real message.
	try
	{

	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// plansAssigned - FIRST PAGE ONLY, a plain count of his open plans.
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	plansAssigned = 0;
	if(firstPage == true)
	{
		plansAssigned = Production_Planning[Assigned_To == supId && (Order_Status == "Pending" || Order_Status == "Material Ready" || Order_Status == "Partially Received" || Order_Status == "In Progress")].count();
	}

	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// What is already in dispute, and therefore NOT waiting to be received.
	//
	// Report 1.5 m missing out of 2.5 and, without this, that 1.5 stays on this
	// screen as an ordinary pending delivery - so it can be received a second
	// time, credited while the dispute is still open, and the item released to
	// production on material nobody has.
	//
	// Keyed per plan+material (not per material) so the per-order detail below
	// still adds up to the total beside it.
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// FIRST PAGE ONLY. Bounded (his open disputes), and the netting it feeds is
	// applied as lines are walked - but a later page continues the same walk, so
	// its share of the netting would be lost. Simplest correct answer: only page
	// 1 nets disputes, and page 1 is where the newest vouchers (the ones a fresh
	// dispute is most likely against) are. A dispute against an old voucher that
	// only a later page reaches is a rare edge; if it bites, the fix is to move
	// dispute-netting into the widget's merge, not to re-fetch disputes per page.
	openDispPM = Map();
	openDispWP = Map();

	dispRows = List();
	if(firstPage == true)
	{
		dispRows = Stock_Dispute[Supervisor == supId && Status == "Open"];
	}
	for each  dsp in dispRows
	{
		dqStr = ifnull(dsp.Disputed_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
		if(dqStr == "")
		{
			dqStr = "0";
		}

		resSoFar = 0.0;
		for each  rl in dsp.Resolution_Lines
		{
			rqStr = ifnull(rl.Resolved_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
			if(rqStr == "")
			{
				rqStr = "0";
			}
			resSoFar = resSoFar + rqStr.toDecimal();
		}

		stillOpen = dqStr.toDecimal() - resSoFar;

		if(stillOpen > 0)
		{
			if(ifnull(dsp.Is_Waste,false) == true && dsp.Waste_Piece != null)
			{
				wKey = dsp.Waste_Piece + "";
				wHave = openDispWP.get(wKey);
				if(wHave == null)
				{
					wHave = 0.0;
				}
				openDispWP.put(wKey,wHave + stillOpen);
			}
			else if(dsp.Plan != null && dsp.Material != null)
			{
				pmKey = dsp.Plan + "|" + dsp.Material;
				pmHave = openDispPM.get(pmKey);
				if(pmHave == null)
				{
					pmHave = 0.0;
				}
				openDispPM.put(pmKey,pmHave + stillOpen);
			}
		}
	}

	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// THE RECEIPT LIST, STRAIGHT OFF THE VOUCHERS.
	//
	// One indexed query for his handovers, then their Issue_Lines. A line is
	// "still owed" when Settled_Qty < Qty - the same test receiveMaterials
	// settles against. Newest voucher first, so when only part of a material is
	// still owed the lot named is the most recent cloth (receipt settles the
	// oldest handover first, so the tail that is left is the newest roll).
	//
	// PRINTED_PIECE lines (marked in Lot_Override_Note) are each one physical
	// printed piece the supervisor receives individually - kept as their own
	// list, not merged into the metres aggregate.
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// mat id -> aggregate Map {matId,name,unit,isFabric,pending,hasReissue}
	agg = Map();
	orderedKeys = List();
	// PER-PLAN ROLL-UP, not per line. "matId|planId" -> Map {planId,planNo,
	// salesOrder,pending,isReissue,reason,lineCount}. ordKeys is matId -> ordered
	// list of its plan keys. One entry per plan a SKU feeds, so a trim across
	// 100 plans is 100 entries - not one JSON fragment per Issue_Line, which at
	// 100 items/order was 10,000 on a single material row.
	ordAgg = Map();
	ordKeys = Map();
	// mat id -> (lot id -> summed still-owed qty), and mat id -> (lot id -> note
	// text). Replaces three "~"-joined parallel strings that grew one entry per
	// line. The old emit walked them "up to adjPending" newest-first; that cap
	// was a no-op (non-printed line pendings already sum to adjPending), so a
	// plain per-lot sum is equivalent.
	lotAgg = Map();
	lotNoteAgg = Map();
	// mat id -> list of distinct voucher ids the material sits on. The widget
	// unions these into the "vouchers" sweep scope it posts back; receiveMaterials
	// walks each voucher's Issue_Lines itself now, so no per-line array is sent.
	vouchByMat = Map();
	// mat id -> metres still owed on printed-piece lines (deducted from agg)
	printedPendByMat = Map();
	// lot id -> readable number, filled lazily
	lotNumById = Map();

	// Requirement id -> "planId|planNo|salesOrder|source|reason", resolved once
	// per DISTINCT requirement actually named on a still-owed line. This is the
	// only place plan/order context is needed, and it is one lookup per pending
	// line at most, never a per-plan row walk.
	reqInfo = Map();

	// THE CURSOR. globalLineIdx counts EVERY Issue_Line of every voucher, in the
	// same order every call sees them (Issued_To filter + Added_Time desc is
	// stable). Lines before skipLines are stepped over without being read;
	// linesProcessed counts what this call actually handled and stops it at
	// rowBudget. linesConsumed in the response is linesProcessed, so the next
	// call's skipLines is skipLines + linesConsumed. 0 means nothing left.
	globalLineIdx = 0;
	linesProcessed = 0;
	budgetSpent = false;

	// sort by on its own assignment, never inline in a for-each header.
	supVouchers = Material_Issue[Issued_To == supId] sort by Added_Time desc;
	for each  miRec in supVouchers
	{
		for each  miLn in miRec.Issue_Lines
		{
			if(budgetSpent == true)
			{
				globalLineIdx = globalLineIdx + 1;
			}
			else if(globalLineIdx < skipLines)
			{
				// Already returned by an earlier page - step over it cheaply.
				globalLineIdx = globalLineIdx + 1;
			}
			else if(linesProcessed >= rowBudget)
			{
				budgetSpent = true;
				globalLineIdx = globalLineIdx + 1;
			}
			else
			{
			globalLineIdx = globalLineIdx + 1;
			linesProcessed = linesProcessed + 1;

			lnMat = ifnull(miLn.Material,"").toString().trim();
			if(lnMat == "")
			{
				continue;
			}

			lqS = ifnull(miLn.Qty,"0").toString().trim();
			if(lqS == "")
			{
				lqS = "0";
			}
			lnQty = lqS.toDecimal();

			setS = ifnull(miLn.Settled_Qty,"0").toString().trim();
			if(setS == "")
			{
				setS = "0";
			}
			lnPend = lnQty - setS.toDecimal();
			// A line settled up to or past its own quantity is done - it must
			// never ADD to an aggregate. receiveMaterials clamps the same way.
			if(lnPend <= 0)
			{
				continue;
			}

			lnReqTxt = ifnull(miLn.Requirement,"").toString().trim();

			// Resolve this line's requirement -> plan / order / source / reason,
			// ONCE per distinct requirement.
			rPlanId = "";
			rPlanNo = "";
			rSalesOrder = "";
			rSource = "Plan";
			rReason = "";
			rIsFab = "";
			if(lnReqTxt != "")
			{
				riCached = ifnull(reqInfo.get(lnReqTxt),"").toString();
				if(riCached == "")
				{
					for each  rq in Material_Requirement[ID == lnReqTxt.toLong()]
					{
						rSource = ifnull(rq.Source,"").toString().trim();
						if(rSource == "")
						{
							rSource = "Plan";
						}
						rIsFab = ifnull(rq.Is_Fabric,false) + "";
						rReason = ifnull(rq.Reason,"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'").replaceAll("\r","").replaceAll("\n"," | ").replaceAll("\t"," ");
						rqPlanTxt = ifnull(rq.Plan,"").toString().trim();
						if(rqPlanTxt != "")
						{
							rPlanId = rqPlanTxt;
							for each  pp in Production_Planning[ID == rqPlanTxt.toLong()]
							{
								rPlanNo = ifnull(pp.Plan_No,"").toString();
								ppSoTxt = ifnull(pp.Sales_Order,"").toString().trim();
								if(ppSoTxt != "")
								{
									for each  ppSo in Sales_Order[ID == ppSoTxt.toLong()]
									{
										rSalesOrder = ifnull(ppSo.Sales_Order,"").toString();
									}
								}
							}
						}
					}
					// planId^planNo^salesOrder^source^isFabric^reason - "^" as
					// separator, reason last and already flattened of quotes /
					// newlines / tabs above so a "^" in it cannot split the cache.
					reqInfo.put(lnReqTxt,rPlanId + "^" + rPlanNo + "^" + rSalesOrder + "^" + rSource + "^" + rIsFab + "^" + rReason);
				}
				else
				{
					riBits = riCached.toList("^");
					if(riBits.size() >= 6)
					{
						rPlanId = riBits.get(0).toString();
						rPlanNo = riBits.get(1).toString();
						rSalesOrder = riBits.get(2).toString();
						rSource = riBits.get(3).toString();
						rIsFab = riBits.get(4).toString();
						rReason = riBits.get(5).toString();
					}
				}
			}

			// This line's plan HAS had material issued - record it for the
			// widget's plansAwaiting union. planFedSeen dedupes within the page.
			if(rPlanId != "" && planFedSeen.contains(rPlanId) == false)
			{
				planFedSeen.add(rPlanId);
				if(planFedJson != "")
				{
					planFedJson = planFedJson + ",";
				}
				planFedJson = planFedJson + "\"" + rPlanId + "\"";
			}

			// Net off whatever of this plan+material is already in dispute -
			// drawn down as applied so two lines cannot each discount it.
			if(rPlanId != "")
			{
				pmKeyL = rPlanId + "|" + lnMat;
				dispLeftL = openDispPM.get(pmKeyL);
				if(dispLeftL != null && dispLeftL > 0)
				{
					takeOffL = dispLeftL;
					if(takeOffL > lnPend)
					{
						takeOffL = lnPend;
					}
					lnPend = lnPend - takeOffL;
					openDispPM.put(pmKeyL,dispLeftL - takeOffL);
				}
			}
			if(lnPend <= 0)
			{
				continue;
			}

			lnNote = ifnull(miLn.Lot_Override_Note,"").toString().trim();
			isRe = "false";
			if(rSource == "Reissue")
			{
				isRe = "true";
			}

			//------------------------------------------------------------
			// PRINTED FABRIC PIECES - one physical piece per line.
			//------------------------------------------------------------
			if(lnNote.contains("PRINTED_PIECE"))
			{
				printedPendByMat.put(lnMat,ifnull(printedPendByMat.get(lnMat),0.0) + lnPend);

				pcLotNum = "Not recorded";
				lnLotTxt = ifnull(miLn.Lot,"").toString().trim();
				if(lnLotTxt != "")
				{
					if(lotNumById.get(lnLotTxt) == null)
					{
						lotNumById.put(lnLotTxt,"");
						for each  lref in Raw_Material_Lot[ID == lnLotTxt.toLong()]
						{
							lotNumById.put(lnLotTxt,ifnull(lref.Lot_Number,"").toString());
						}
					}
					pcLotNum = ifnull(lotNumById.get(lnLotTxt),"").toString();
					if(pcLotNum == "")
					{
						pcLotNum = "Not recorded";
					}
				}

				pcName = "";
				pcUnit = "";
				pcAgg = agg.get(lnMat);
				if(pcAgg != null)
				{
					pcName = ifnull(pcAgg.get("name"),"").toString();
					pcUnit = ifnull(pcAgg.get("unit"),"").toString();
				}
				else
				{
					pcName = ifnull(miLn.Material_Name,"").toString();
					pcUnit = ifnull(miLn.Unit,"").toString();
				}

				if(printedPiecesJson != "")
				{
					printedPiecesJson = printedPiecesJson + ",";
				}
				printedPiecesJson = printedPiecesJson + "{\"issueLineId\":\"" + miLn.ID + "\",\"voucherId\":\"" + miRec.ID + "\",\"materialId\":\"" + lnMat + "\",\"material\":\"" + pcName.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"unit\":\"" + pcUnit + "\",\"qty\":" + lnQty + ",\"pending\":" + lnPend + ",\"cutWidth\":" + ifnull(miLn.Cut_Size_Width,0) + ",\"cutLength\":" + ifnull(miLn.Cut_Size_Length,0) + ",\"planNo\":\"" + rPlanNo.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"salesOrder\":\"" + rSalesOrder.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"lot\":\"" + pcLotNum.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"planId\":\"" + rPlanId + "\"}";
				continue;
			}

			//------------------------------------------------------------
			// REGULAR MATERIAL - merged into the per-material aggregate.
			//------------------------------------------------------------
			// isFabric off the REQUIREMENT (via reqInfo), not a cut-size guess -
			// a fabric row planned before Required_Pieces existed can carry a
			// 0x0 cut size. Falls back to the cut-size heuristic only when the
			// line names no requirement.
			lnIsFab = "false";
			if(rIsFab != "")
			{
				lnIsFab = rIsFab;
			}
			else if(ifnull(miLn.Cut_Size_Width,0) > 0 || ifnull(miLn.Cut_Size_Length,0) > 0)
			{
				lnIsFab = "true";
			}

			cur = agg.get(lnMat);
			if(cur == null)
			{
				cur = Map();
				cur.put("matId",lnMat);
				cur.put("name",ifnull(miLn.Material_Name,"").toString());
				cur.put("unit",ifnull(miLn.Unit,"").toString());
				cur.put("isFabric",lnIsFab);
				cur.put("pending",0.0);
				cur.put("hasReissue","false");
				agg.put(lnMat,cur);
				orderedKeys.add(lnMat);
			}
			cur.put("pending",cur.get("pending") + lnPend);
			if(isRe == "true")
			{
				cur.put("hasReissue","true");
			}
			agg.put(lnMat,cur);

			// PER-PLAN ROLL-UP. One accumulator per plan this material feeds, not
			// one JSON fragment per Issue_Line. rPlanId "" (requirement resolved
			// no plan) rolls into a single "matId|" bucket.
			pKeyM = lnMat + "|" + rPlanId;
			oCur = ordAgg.get(pKeyM);
			if(oCur == null)
			{
				oCur = Map();
				oCur.put("planId",rPlanId);
				oCur.put("planNo",rPlanNo);
				oCur.put("salesOrder",rSalesOrder);
				oCur.put("pending",0.0);
				oCur.put("isReissue","false");
				oCur.put("reason","");
				oCur.put("lineCount",0);
				ordAgg.put(pKeyM,oCur);
				okList = ordKeys.get(lnMat);
				if(okList == null)
				{
					okList = List();
				}
				okList.add(pKeyM);
				ordKeys.put(lnMat,okList);
			}
			oCur.put("pending",oCur.get("pending") + lnPend);
			oCur.put("lineCount",oCur.get("lineCount") + 1);
			if(isRe == "true")
			{
				oCur.put("isReissue","true");
			}
			if(ifnull(oCur.get("reason"),"").toString() == "" && rReason != "")
			{
				oCur.put("reason",rReason);
			}
			ordAgg.put(pKeyM,oCur);

			// PER-LOT ROLL-UP. lot id -> summed still-owed qty for this material.
			// Inner map pulled into a variable before .put - Deluge cannot chain
			// a method onto a Map.get() result.
			lidM = ifnull(miLn.Lot,"").toString().trim();
			if(lidM == "")
			{
				lidM = "none";
			}
			lMap = lotAgg.get(lnMat);
			if(lMap == null)
			{
				lMap = Map();
			}
			lMap.put(lidM,ifnull(lMap.get(lidM),0.0) + lnPend);
			lotAgg.put(lnMat,lMap);
			if(lnNote != "")
			{
				nMap = lotNoteAgg.get(lnMat);
				if(nMap == null)
				{
					nMap = Map();
				}
				haveN = ifnull(nMap.get(lidM),"").toString();
				if(haveN.contains(lnNote) == false)
				{
					if(haveN != "")
					{
						haveN = haveN + ", ";
					}
					nMap.put(lidM,haveN + lnNote);
					lotNoteAgg.put(lnMat,nMap);
				}
			}

			// Distinct vouchers this material sits on.
			vList = vouchByMat.get(lnMat);
			if(vList == null)
			{
				vList = List();
			}
			vIdTxt = miRec.ID + "";
			if(vList.contains(vIdTxt) == false)
			{
				vList.add(vIdTxt);
			}
			vouchByMat.put(lnMat,vList);
			}
			// end of the "within this page's budget" else
		}
	}

	// linesConsumed for the response cursor: what this call actually processed.
	// 0 when skipLines was already past the end - the widget stops there.
	linesConsumed = linesProcessed;

	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// WASTE PIECES - listed individually, off HIS Issued movements. Moved_By is
	// the supervisor, so no plan walk: one indexed query, then its Received
	// children per movement. FIRST PAGE ONLY - bounded, and the widget carries
	// it through the merge unchanged.
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	wasteMoves = List();
	if(firstPage == true)
	{
		wasteMoves = Waste_Movement[Moved_By == supId && Movement_Type == "Issued"];
	}
	for each  wi in wasteMoves
	{
		wCount = ifnull(wi.Piece_Count,0);

		wRecv = 0;
		for each  rv in Waste_Movement[Parent_Movement == wi.ID && Movement_Type == "Received"]
		{
			wRecv = wRecv + ifnull(rv.Piece_Count,0);
		}
		wPend = wCount - wRecv;

		wKey2 = wi.Waste_Piece + "";
		wDispLeft = openDispWP.get(wKey2);
		if(wDispLeft != null && wDispLeft > 0)
		{
			wTakeOff = wDispLeft;
			if(wTakeOff > wPend)
			{
				wTakeOff = wPend;
			}
			wPend = wPend - wTakeOff.toLong();
			openDispWP.put(wKey2,wDispLeft - wTakeOff);
		}

		if(wPend > 0)
		{
			wSkuId = "";
			wMatName = "";
			for each  wmRec in Waste_Master[ID == wi.Waste_Piece]
			{
				wSkuId = ifnull(wmRec.SKU,"").toString();
			}
			if(wSkuId != "")
			{
				for each  wrm in Raw_Material[ID == wSkuId.toLong()]
				{
					wMatName = ifnull(wrm.Material_Display_Name,"").toString().trim();
					if(wMatName == "")
					{
						wMatName = ifnull(wrm.Name,"").toString().trim();
					}
					if(wMatName == "")
					{
						wMatName = ifnull(wrm.SKU,"").toString();
					}
				}
			}

			wPlanNo = "";
			wSo = "";
			wiPlanTxt = ifnull(wi.Plan,"").toString().trim();
			if(wiPlanTxt != "")
			{
				for each  wpp in Production_Planning[ID == wiPlanTxt.toLong()]
				{
					wPlanNo = ifnull(wpp.Plan_No,"").toString();
					wppSoTxt = ifnull(wpp.Sales_Order,"").toString().trim();
					if(wppSoTxt != "")
					{
						for each  wppSo in Sales_Order[ID == wppSoTxt.toLong()]
						{
							wSo = ifnull(wppSo.Sales_Order,"").toString();
						}
					}
				}
			}

			if(wasteJson != "")
			{
				wasteJson = wasteJson + ",";
			}
			wasteJson = wasteJson + "{\"rowId\":\"" + wi.ID + "\",\"planId\":\"" + wiPlanTxt + "\",\"planNo\":\"" + wPlanNo.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"salesOrder\":\"" + wSo.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"materialId\":\"" + wSkuId + "\",\"material\":\"" + wMatName.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"width\":" + ifnull(wi.Piece_Width,0) + ",\"length\":" + ifnull(wi.Piece_Length,0) + ",\"pending\":" + wPend + ",\"cutWidth\":" + ifnull(wi.Cut_Size_Width,0) + ",\"cutLength\":" + ifnull(wi.Cut_Size_Length,0) + ",\"yields\":" + ifnull(wi.Pieces_Yielded,0) + "}";
		}
	}

	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	// EMIT. Per material: the aggregate, its per-plan order roll-up, the per-lot
	// breakdown, and the distinct vouchers it sits on (the widget's sweep scope).
	//------------------------------------------------------------------------
	for each  k in orderedKeys
	{
		eAgg = agg.get(k);

		adjPending = eAgg.get("pending") - ifnull(printedPendByMat.get(k),0.0);
		if(adjPending <= 0)
		{
			continue;
		}

		// --- lots: straight off the per-lot roll-up ---
		lotsJson = "";
		kLotMap = lotAgg.get(k);
		kNoteMap = lotNoteAgg.get(k);
		if(kLotMap != null)
		{
			lotKeys = kLotMap.keys();
			for each  lotKey in lotKeys
			{
				lotVal = kLotMap.get(lotKey);
				if(lotVal > 0)
				{
					lotLabelTxt = "Not recorded";
					if(lotKey != "none")
					{
						if(lotNumById.get(lotKey) == null)
						{
							lotNumById.put(lotKey,"");
							for each  lotRef in Raw_Material_Lot[ID == lotKey.toLong()]
							{
								lotNumById.put(lotKey,ifnull(lotRef.Lot_Number,"").toString());
							}
						}
						lotLabelTxt = ifnull(lotNumById.get(lotKey),"").toString();
						if(lotLabelTxt == "")
						{
							lotLabelTxt = "Not recorded";
						}
					}

					nTxt = "";
					if(kNoteMap != null)
					{
						nTxt = ifnull(kNoteMap.get(lotKey),"").toString();
					}
					if(nTxt != "")
					{
						lotLabelTxt = lotLabelTxt + " (" + nTxt + ")";
					}

					if(lotsJson != "")
					{
						lotsJson = lotsJson + ",";
					}
					lotsJson = lotsJson + "{\"lot\":\"" + lotLabelTxt.replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"qty\":" + lotVal + "}";
				}
			}
		}

		// --- orders: one entry per plan this material feeds ---
		ordersJson = "";
		kOrdKeys = ordKeys.get(k);
		if(kOrdKeys != null)
		{
			for each  ok in kOrdKeys
			{
				oe = ordAgg.get(ok);
				if(oe != null)
				{
					if(ordersJson != "")
					{
						ordersJson = ordersJson + ",";
					}
					// reason was flattened of quotes / newlines / tabs where it
					// was built (reqInfo), so it needs no re-escape here.
					ordersJson = ordersJson + "{\"planId\":\"" + ifnull(oe.get("planId"),"").toString() + "\",\"planNo\":\"" + ifnull(oe.get("planNo"),"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"salesOrder\":\"" + ifnull(oe.get("salesOrder"),"").toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"pending\":" + ifnull(oe.get("pending"),0.0) + ",\"isReissue\":" + ifnull(oe.get("isReissue"),"false") + ",\"reason\":\"" + ifnull(oe.get("reason"),"").toString() + "\",\"lineCount\":" + ifnull(oe.get("lineCount"),0) + "}";
				}
			}
		}

		// --- voucher ids this material sits on ---
		vJson = "";
		kV = vouchByMat.get(k);
		if(kV != null)
		{
			for each  vv in kV
			{
				if(vJson != "")
				{
					vJson = vJson + ",";
				}
				vJson = vJson + "\"" + vv + "\"";
			}
		}

		if(matJson != "")
		{
			matJson = matJson + ",";
		}
		matJson = matJson + "{\"materialId\":\"" + eAgg.get("matId") + "\",\"material\":\"" + eAgg.get("name").toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + "\",\"unit\":\"" + eAgg.get("unit") + "\",\"isFabric\":" + eAgg.get("isFabric") + ",\"isReissue\":" + ifnull(eAgg.get("hasReissue"),"false") + ",\"pending\":" + eAgg.get("pending") + ",\"lots\":[" + lotsJson + "],\"orders\":[" + ordersJson + "],\"voucherIds\":[" + vJson + "]}";
	}

	}
	catch (e)
	{
		info "getSupervisorMaterials DELUGE ERROR: " + e.toString();
		// linesConsumed:0 so the widget's page loop stops rather than spinning
		// on a failing call for ever.
		return "{\"errors\":[\"" + e.toString().replaceAll("\"","'") + "\"],\"supervisors\":[" + supJson + "],\"materials\":[],\"waste\":[],\"printedPieces\":[],\"planFed\":[],\"plansAssigned\":0,\"linesConsumed\":0,\"skipLines\":" + skipLines + "}";
	}

	// Built by hand - List.toString() does not reliably wrap in [].
	//
	// plansAwaiting is NOT here - the widget computes it from plansAssigned (page
	// 1) minus the union of every page's planFed. linesConsumed is the cursor:
	// next call's skipLines is skipLines + linesConsumed; 0 means done.
	return "{\"errors\":[],\"supervisors\":[" + supJson + "],\"materials\":[" + matJson + "],\"waste\":[" + wasteJson + "],\"printedPieces\":[" + printedPiecesJson + "],\"planFed\":[" + planFedJson + "],\"plansAssigned\":" + plansAssigned + ",\"linesConsumed\":" + linesConsumed + ",\"skipLines\":" + skipLines + "}";
}
